sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Administrator
    actor R as Ravi (trainer)
    participant B as Ravi's browser
    participant G as Gateway
    participant RD as Redis
    participant I as identity-service
    participant K as Kafka
    participant NO as notification-service
    participant S as Any service

    Note over A,I: The administrator gives Ravi the Coordinator duty
    A->>I: PUT /api/users/7/duties {extraRoles: [COORDINATOR]} (ADMIN only)
    I->>I: refuse a student, an admin, TRAINER, or the main role repeated
    I->>I: save extra_roles, roles_version 0 -> 1
    I->>RD: SET rv:7 = 1
    I->>K: user-updated (with the extra duties)
    K->>NO: directory keeps the duties, so role notifications reach Ravi
    I->>K: audit.recorded (USER_DUTIES_CHANGED), notification "Your duties changed"
    I-->>A: Ravi, now with + Coordinator

    Note over R,S: Ravi keeps working with a token issued before the change (rv = 0)
    R->>B: clicks anything
    B->>G: request with the old token
    G->>G: verify signature and expiry
    G->>RD: GET rv:7
    RD-->>G: 1
    G-->>B: 401 PERMISSIONS_CHANGED (1 is newer than 0)
    B->>G: POST /api/auth/refresh (the app does this by itself)
    G->>I: forward
    I->>I: read the person from the database
    I-->>B: new token with xr = [COORDINATOR], rv = 1, and the user with extraRoles
    B->>B: store.roles = [TRAINER, COORDINATOR], the sidebar and guards follow
    B->>G: the same request again, new token
    G->>RD: GET rv:7 (1 = 1, current)
    G->>S: forward
    S->>S: hasAnyRole(ADMIN, COORDINATOR) matches the COORDINATOR authority
    S-->>B: the answer a coordinator gets

    Note over A,I: Withdrawn the same way: roles_version 1 -> 2, the next request is renewed without the duty
    Note over G,RD: If Redis cannot be reached the check is skipped, and the 30-minute token limit still applies
